  "doc_revision": "Eastron SDM230Modbus Smart Meter Modbus Protocol Implementation V1.4 (page headers read 'Eastron SDM230Modbus Protocol V1.3'). Both URLs returned byte-identical files.",
  "verified": false,
  "notes": "Built only from the Eastron protocol PDF above (the user manual 'SDM230 Modbus v2' on docs.vekto.nl contains no register map and was not used for registers). Addressing: the document lists register numbers (3xxxx input, 4xxxx holding) and the protocol start address in hex. This preset uses address_base 0 and the PROTOCOL address = input register number minus 30001 (30073 -> 72 = 0x0048) / holding register number minus 40001 (40021 -> 20 = 0x0014); all cross-checked against the hex column. The F9xx / FCxx rows use the doc's hex column: the doc's decimal register numbers for 'Measurement mode' (463776) and 'Running time' (463792) are inconsistent with their hex (F920 / F930) so hex was used; 463761 -> 0xF910 and 464513 -> 0xFC00 match. Data: 32-bit IEEE754 float, 'most significant register first (default)' (a 'Register Order' holding parameter is mentioned but no address is given, so it is not included). Doc limits: max 40 values (80 registers) per request, requests must be even-aligned pairs. NOTE the tool's block merger allows up to 125 registers per read, which exceeds this device limit: read groups separately (e.g. group='measure') or keep the point set small. Defaults per the doc: node address 1, parity/stop code 0 (1 stop, no parity), baud code 0 = 2400 bps (default); doc says selectable baud 1200/2400/4800/9600; baud/parity/ID need a restart. Left out: 'Reset' register 461457 (0xF010, write-only, 0000 = reset max demand, 0003 = reset resettable energy), the BCD-format 'Demand interval/scroll/backlight' register 0xF500, and 'Running time' (0xF930). Not verified against a physical device. max_block=40: the protocol document limits one request to 40 values (80 registers).",
